./md-review-records/2026-08-04-d-review-skill-self-review/claude-restate-floor.md:153:13. "Codex-runtime cells run through `scripts/d-review-codex-cell.py` — one invocation per cell (`--cell restate|defect-hunt --tier good|floor --target <path>`), headless `codex exec`, read-only sandbox, the cell's final message on stdout." — For the Codex runtime, each cell is executed via one separate invocation of the named script, configured with --cell, --tier, and --target arguments, run headlessly via codex exec inside a read-only sandbox, with the cell's final message delivered on standard output.
./md-review-records/2026-08-04-d-review-skill-self-review/claude-restate-floor.md:155:15. "The tier-to-model mapping and per-tier reasoning effort sit at the top of the script (authoritative; any ids quoted in prose are a snapshot), currently `gpt-5.6-sol` / `gpt-5.6-terra` at `xhigh`, boss-picked and live-verified 2026-08-03, pinned in the script so a cell does not depend on the machine-local Codex config." — States that the authoritative tier-to-model mapping and reasoning-effort setting live at the top of the referenced script (with any model IDs quoted in prose being only a point-in-time snapshot), currently gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-5.6-terra at "xhigh" effort, chosen by the boss and confirmed working on 2026-08-03, and hard-coded in the script so cell behavior does not depend on the local machine's Codex configuration.
