./md-review-records/2026-08-11-ghi-info-agent-design/claude-hunt-good.md:59:**28. `the next refresh carries it into the corpus, and answers reflect it after the next reload — a lag bounded by the recycle triggers` (line 69)** — The resume prompt already hands the agent changed entries every turn: "these mirror entries changed: #<n>, #<m>. Re-read them in the mirror before answering" (line 208). An added cross-link is a body edit, which moves the issue's `updated` timestamp (line 291) and therefore appears in the delta, so the correction is visible on the very next ask, not at the next reload. Harm: the stated lag bound is longer than the mechanism's actual behavior, which will mislead anyone reasoning about self-correction speed or tuning the recycle thresholds. Confidence: unsure — it depends on the line 291 timestamp assumption, which the file itself lists as untested.
