./md-review-records/2026-08-09-ghi-info-agent-design-2/codex-hunt-floor.md:53:26. `“nedsmessenger runs this exact pattern live”` is false relative to its explicitly cited `adapter.py`. That implementation injects first-call channel history and uses separate idle-silence, in-flight-tool-silence, and total-runtime watchdog conditions, while this design specifies one overall timeout. Calling the patterns exact hides a material operational difference. Confidence: sure.
./md-review-records/2026-08-09-ghi-info-agent-design-2/claude-hunt-good.md:16:Script *execution* is free of agent tokens, but everything the scripts produce is consumed by the agent: the whole open-issues mirror enters context on every cold start, and the ~109 KB figure at line 28 is the size of that payload. The claim is repeated as the "free" cost column in the Division of labor table and as "Refreshing is fast and cheap" at line 36. Harm: this is the load-bearing economic argument for the whole design ("Mechanical work never spends agent tokens"), so an agent sizing recycle thresholds or corpus growth against it will budget as if reloads cost nothing, when a reload is the single largest token event in the system. Sure.
