docs/agents/sidebar-instructions.md:17:- **Own nothing.** If a question turns into real project work, do not adopt it — name the seat it belongs to (`gatekeeper`, `sanity-checker`, `skill-builder`, `ghi`, `fleet`, `doctrine`) and let the user take it there with its context intact.
docs/agents/sidebar-instructions.md:18:- **Say when you are the wrong agent.** A question needing deep history from another pile is better answered by that seat, and saying so quickly is more useful than a shallow answer assembled here.
docs/agents/sidebar-instructions.md:24:The project's standing rules apply here as everywhere: durable artifacts are written for a reader with zero context; instruction-class files (CLAUDE.md, `.claude/` machinery) change only through the user's walked approval; commits carry the session id; nothing is pushed to main, since the Mac-side seat reviews and merges.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:1:# `gatekeeper` — seat instructions
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:3:Your pile: **taking the git-gatekeeper from built-but-dormant to live.** Every task here shares one specification, one program, and one threat model, so each makes the next cheaper. Read [the seat model](agent-seat-model.md) for how seats work; this file is your brief.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:7:`scripts/git-gatekeeper.py` is **built through all five slices** and merged to main (PR #49, 2026-08-12), with a 169-case suite in `scripts/git-gatekeeper-test.py`. The gate is **dormant**: no host holds a main-capable credential, so nothing routes through it yet. Agents currently reach main the interim way — commit to a working branch, push, and the user's Mac-side seat reviews and merges.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:9:**Read first:** `docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md` (the canonical specification, design-as-of 2026-08-12) and `docs/issues/3-git-gatekeeper-build-slice-plan.md` (the build order, its ruled design points, and the program follow-ups). Issue: [nedschorus#3](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/3), whose body is current as of 2026-08-12.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:11:The full review history — two md-review grids, a subtraction review, and every ruling with its reasoning — is in `md-review-records/2026-08-09-git-gatekeeper-design/`. Consult `dispositions.md` and `codex-dispositions.md` there **before reopening any settled question**; roughly forty decisions are recorded with dates and grounds, and re-deriving them wastes the user's time.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:16:2. **Build slice 6** — the review-evidence check, which enforces that format at the gate. Ruled 2026-08-10 as a prerequisite of activation, because the deployed gatekeeper copy self-updates from main and that is only safe once its own source cannot reach main without walked approval.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:19:Also yours: **PR #55** (`gatekeeper audit: account names compared case-insensitively; PR #49 review rulings folded into the slice plan`), open and awaiting review.
docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md:31:Read the specification and the slice plan, check whether PR #55 has merged, then report to the user where the road stands and ask which step he wants first. Do not start the evidence-format design without his go-ahead: it is instruction-class work and its shape is his ruling to make.
