docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md-183-
docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md:184:- **Cross-machine callers (C8):** the gatekeeper reads declared content from the caller's worktree, which requires a shared filesystem; Mac-side agents cannot be read from the Ubuntu box. Candidate shapes, none chosen: the caller pushes its branch and the request names a ref instead of relying on worktree bytes (a real contract change); Mac agents route work through the Ubuntu side; or a second credentialed host (weakens the single-place property of C2). Decide when a Mac-side agent first needs direct check-in.
docs/cross-project/git-gatekeeper-design.md:185:- The walked-approval evidence format (what walked approval looks like as a checkable artifact) — undesigned; slice 6 waits on it.
