docs/cross-project/fast-handoff-design.md-64-- Pre-seed rides undocumented harness state; detection is the ignition count-check, the queues are the backstop, the `--canary` cases are the diagnosis (accepted risk, user-ruled 2026-08-12).
docs/cross-project/fast-handoff-design.md-65-- Very-long-session material can predate the word-floor window and every durable store; bounded by commit-as-you-go and the full-JSONL pointer in every extract. A live thread longer than the floor hands over a partial thread, bounded by the header's left-behind count.
docs/cross-project/fast-handoff-design.md:66:- A supervisor is a per-agent process; if it dies, nothing watches until the next threshold crossing, when the hook-fired skill run starts an adopting supervisor (self-healing since 2026-08-12; `handoff-supervisor.py --check --agent <name>` reports liveness on demand).
